#: ../../guide/languages.md:51
msgid "Checking Languages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:53
msgid ""
"The spell-check and grammar-check language is separate from the file type. "
"Click the language indicator in the VS Code status bar to switch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:55
msgid "**EN-US** — American English"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:56
msgid "**EN-GB** — British English"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:57
msgid "**DE-DE** — German"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:58
msgid "**FR** — French"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:59
msgid "**ES** — Spanish"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:61
msgid ""
"Language detection can also be automatic via the [whatlang](https://"
"crates.io/crates/whatlang) crate when no explicit language is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:63
msgid "More than one language in one file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:65
msgid ""
"`engines.spell_language` is the document default, not the only answer. A "
"thesis in French quoting English, or a German paper with an English "
"abstract, is checked passage by passage: the prose is grouped by language "
"and each group goes to the engines that read it, so Harper handles the "
"English while LanguageTool handles the French."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:71
msgid "Three things declare a language, strongest first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:73
msgid ""
"**A region directive.** Works in every format, and is the only option where "
"the markup has nothing to say:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:82
msgid "**A scope marker**, which runs until the next one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:88
msgid "**The markup's own declaration**, where the format has one. Typst does:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:95
msgid ""
"That last one needs no extra annotation at all — the `lang:` an author "
"already writes for hyphenation and quotation marks is the one the checker "
"reads, and `region:` becomes the BCP-47 subtag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:99
msgid ""
"See the [directives reference](../reference/directives.md) for the full "
"syntax, and [`examples/typst/`](https://github.com/KaiErikNiermann/LangCheck/"
"tree/main/examples/typst) for a worked document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:103
msgid "When nothing can read the language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:105
msgid ""
"Not every language has an engine. LanguageTool has no Hebrew and no Latin, "
"and Harper reads only English. Rather than let the passage pass as clean, "
"the checker reports a `languagecheck.no-provider` diagnostic naming the "
"language, and does not mark the engine unhealthy for declining one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:110
msgid ""
"For most of those, [Hunspell](hunspell-setup.md) fills the gap with spelling "
"— Hebrew, Latin, Welsh, Old English and a long tail besides, using the "
"dictionary format LibreOffice and Firefox already read. It checks spelling "
"and nothing else, so where LanguageTool supports a language, prefer it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:115
msgid ""
"In VS Code the editor offers to install a dictionary when it meets a "
"language none of the enabled engines read, and remembers a refusal. An "
"engine that declares the language answers for it, so a custom "
"`engines.external` checker naming `languages: [\"cy\"]` covers Welsh and the "
"offer never appears — but one that declares nothing at all still claims "
"every language, and suppresses the offer for all of them. See [External "
"providers](../advanced/providers.md) for what a provider should declare."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:124
msgid "Bare tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:126
msgid ""
"A declaration with no region is resolved before it reaches the engines: it "
"takes the document default's region when the language agrees, so `lang: "
"\"en\"` under an `en-GB` document means `en-GB`, and a known variant "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/languages.md:130
msgid ""
"This is not cosmetic. LanguageTool accepts bare `en` and `de` and then "
"reports no spelling errors at all in them, so an unresolved tag would check "
"nothing and look clean."
msgstr ""
